A||||2||Fformula88||Fierostore steering wheel... anybody get it?||||1||
Z||000000||Fformula88||05-31-2001||09:25 PM||||The Fierostore is carrying replica GT leather steering wheels.  I was wondering if anybody has gotten one?  Its not their reconditioned one.  It says it will bolt up to any three spoke equipped car.<P>I am wondering if it comes with the center horn buttom or if you have to use one off an original Fiero wheel.  Also, I was wondering how the quality is on it.<P>Finally, I have a 4 spoke wheel in my Formula, and don't know if it would be compatable or not.  It sounds like I would have to get a 3-spoke wheel first, then use parts from it to make this 3-spoke work.<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG"> <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000001||Bob Englert||05-31-2001||09:29 PM||||I don't know about the Fiero Store wheel (I am also interested), but I do know the 3 spoke and 4 spoke wheels are completely interchangeable.  We took the 4 spoke wheel of my daughter's 87 coupe and installed a 3 spoke wheel out of an 84 SE at the junk yard.  Just be sure to take the wheel, the horn button, and the plastic tube in the wheel that connects the horn to the column and you should be all set!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||05-31-2001||10:06 PM||||88, if I am correct, those wheels are made by a fellow out here in California (seems like I have his email somewhere and will find it if you want it) (in fact, he may very well be a Forum member.........)From what I understand, they will bolt up exactly like the original although it is difficult to tell from the picture just how the horn button will fit on - it looks like those are "flat" in the center rather than recessed and "keyed" like the originals........||||reg||1
